<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore November M1 rises 8.3 pct on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore November M1 rises 8.3 pct on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>				 Nov	Oct	  Nov 95</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 26.51    26.09	24.48</p>
<p>M-2			   110.92   108.70     100.30</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 137.90   135.63     126.68</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    16.53    16.23	14.92</p>
<p>Currency in active	  9.98     9.86	 9.56</p>
<p>circulation  </p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 8.3 percent year-on-year in November, compared with 6.5 percent in October.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
